WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.189
Decide what you can lose. A risk

2
00:00:02.189 --> 00:00:04.066
budget is the planned loss on one

3
00:00:04.066 --> 00:00:07.241
trade, not the cash spent buying shares.

4
00:00:07.641 --> 00:00:10.636
Start with a simple example. 1%

5
00:00:10.636 --> 00:00:13.112
of a $1,000 practice account is

6
00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:15.395
a $10 planned risk budget.

7
00:00:15.808 --> 00:00:18.786
Measure the stop distance. A $100

8
00:00:18.786 --> 00:00:21.161
entry and $98 stop give

9
00:00:21.161 --> 00:00:23.482
a $2 planned loss per share.

10
00:00:23.891 --> 00:00:26.828
Calculate the share count. $10 risk

11
00:00:26.828 --> 00:00:28.997
budget divided by $2 per share

12
00:00:28.997 --> 00:00:32.340
gives 5 shares, costing $500 to

13
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.164
buy.

14
00:00:33.564 --> 00:00:36.261
Allow for uncertainty. A real stop can

15
00:00:36.261 --> 00:00:39.040
